    "title": "When is March Madness Selection Sunday? Time, date, TV for bracket",
    "text": "Updated March 11, 2026, 10:16 p.m. ETWhen is Selection Sunday show time? And when is the 2026 March Madness bracket revealed?The answers for the 2026 NCAA Tournament for men's basketball haven't changed from previous years.Selection Sunday is this Sunday, March 15, with a scheduled start time of 6 p.m. ET. The show will be hosted on CBS and streamed on Fubo, which offers a free trial to potential subsribers.The 68-team men's NCAA Tournament field opens Tuesday, March 17, with the playing of the First Four in Dayton, Ohio.Watch Selection Sunday live on Fubo (free trial)The women's basketball tournament selection show time is at 8 p.m. ET Sunday, March 15, on ESPN, with play beginning Wednesday, March 18.Here's what to know about when the March Madness bracket is being revealed, the NCAA Tournament men's basketball schedule and much more.When is Selection Sunday 2026?Date: Sunday, March 15.The Selection Sunday show date for men's basketball is Sunday for the 2026 NCAA Tournament.What time is March Madness bracket released?Selection Sunday show time: 6 p.m. ETThe field of 68 for the 2026 men's basketball NCAA Tournament is scheduled to be revealed region-by-region beginning at 6 p.m. ET on Sunday.What channel is Selection Sunday show?TV channel: CBS.Streaming option: Fubo (free trial).CBS will televise the 2026 men's NCAA Tournament Selection Sunday show on Sunday, March 15, at approximately 6 p.m. ET. (This could be delayed if the 3:30 p.m. Big Ten Tournament championship game goes long.)The streaming options for the men's March Madness Selection Sunday show are Fubo, which carries CBS and offers a free trial to new subscribers, and Paramount+.March Madness schedule 2026Start date: Tuesday, March 17 (First Four).End date: Monday, April 6 (national championship).March Madness officially gets underway on Tuesday, March 17 in Dayton, Ohio, at UD Arena with the first set of two games in the First Four matchups. Two more games are played Wednesday.The first round is played Thursday and Friday at eight different sites around the United States: Buffalo, Greenville, Oklahoma City, Philadelphia, Portland, San Diego, St. Louis and Tampa.The regional semifinals and finals are at four cities: Chicago (Midwest), Houston (South), San Jose (West) and Washington, DC (East).The men's NCAA Tournament concludes with the Final Four on Saturday, April 4, in Indianapolis, and the national championship game is Monday, April 6.Here is the full schedule breakdown for the 2026 NCAA Tournament:First Four: Tuesday, March 17-Wednesday, March 18.First round: Thursday, March 19-Friday, March 20.Second round: Saturday, March 21-Sunday, March 22.Sweet 16: Thursday, March 26-Friday, March 27 (Chicago, Houston, San Jose, Washington).Elite Eight: Saturday, March 28-Sunday, March 29 (Chicago, Houston, San Jose, Washington).Final Four: Saturday, April 4 (Indianapolis).National championship game: Monday, April 6 (Indianapolis).",
